{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115027","id":3180616821,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc69lFx1","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115027","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115027.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115027.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115027","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115027/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115027/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115027/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8183952e89a7093477cf0e3447497cc4a0fd635b","number":115027,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Implement motion blur feature based on the community plugin","user":{"login":"HydrogenC","id":33123710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzNzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33123710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC","html_url":"https://github.com/HydrogenC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HydrogenC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR implements the motion blur post processing based on the community plugin created by @sphynx-owner . The original repos could be found here: https://github.com/sphynx-owner/godot-motion-blur-addon-simplified and https://github.com/sphynx-owner/JFA_driven_motion_blur_addon. \r\nCloses [godotengine/godot-proposals#12258](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12258) and <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2933>.\r\nThere are some differences compared to the original plugin, notably:\r\n\r\n- * Cleaning up of unused resources in shader\r\n- * Cleaning up the code\r\n- * Changed some uniform constants to specification constants, enabling loop unrolling, so the performance is better\r\n\r\nThis PR is co-authored with @AR-DEV-1 , with me doing the graphics and shaders part and @AR-DEV-1 working with the editor settings parts. \r\nSupported backend: Forward+.\r\n\r\nPreview: \r\n<img width=\"1454\" height=\"1149\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ecb7c7f3-7b76-4126-b8f7-381c31210f6a\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n<del>Docs not yet written, since the API itself may be subject to change during review. Docs will be finished by @AR-DEV-1 after the API itself gets approved. </del>  \r\nThe current blocker is that the current implementation exposes too many parameters, we may have to scale the number down and make some of them constant instead. \r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> `godot-cpp` will also be modified with these changes after the the API itself gets approved. The build for the editor with mono on Linux can be ignored for now. \r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> This PR has used AI for reviewing the code but only in commit https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115027/commits/caa3901fda7798816481c3b60f0ca7c8fe5ff475, the code is all written by humans\r\n\r\n_(the above was written in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115027#issuecomment-4876006287)_","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","na